<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Blood River</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1838</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Ncome</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Blood River was fought on 16 December 1838 on the Ncome River in Natal between about 470 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-pretorius">Andries Pretorius</a> and a much larger army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingane">Dingane</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a>. Defending a wagon laager with firearms, the Voortrekkers killed some 3,000 Zulu without losing a man. The victory led to the founding of the Natalia Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-blood-river.jpg" alt="Battle of Blood River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Renier Maritz · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bloedrivier_monument.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
